15 0 obj
<< /A 43 0 R /Alt (Three-panel figure showing time-dependent ROC curves for nine models at 24, 36, and 48 months. Each panel displays sensitivity versus 1 minus specificity, with model names and AUC values listed in the legend.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 44 0 R /Alt (Panel A is a calibration plot for Ridge model predictions at 24 months, panel B at 36 months, and panel C at 48 months. Each plot shows observed risk versus mean predicted risk, with a diagonal dashed line representing perfect calibration and a turquoise line representing model performance.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 35 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 45 0 R /Alt (Three line graphs labeled A, B, and C display decision curve analysis \(DCA\) of net benefit versus threshold probability for Ridge models at 24, 36, and 48 months, respectively. Each graph compares three lines: Ridge model \(blue\), treat all \(yellow-green\), and none \(dark purple, flat at zero\). The Ridge model outperforms or matches treat-all for most thresholds, with net benefit declining as threshold increases. All axes are clearly labeled.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 46 0 R /Alt (Panel A, B, and C display time-dependent receiver operating characteristic \(ROC\) curves comparing the performance of nine statistical and machine learning models at 12, 24, and 36 months, respectively, for survival prediction. The area under the curve \(AUC\) values for each model are listed in the legends. Sensitivity and 1-specificity are plotted on the y- and x-axes, with higher curves indicating better model performance.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 36 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
19 0 obj
<< /A 47 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a calibration plot at twelve months for an ExtraTrees model with observed risk versus mean predicted risk, where the data fluctuates around but often deviates from the diagonal reference line. Panel B depicts a calibration plot at twenty-four months for a Ridge model, demonstrating observed risk versus mean predicted risk, with data points displaying moderate alignment to the diagonal reference. Panel C presents a calibration plot at thirty-six months for a Ridge model, with observed risk versus mean predicted risk, where the values trend closer to the reference line but show variability.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
20 0 obj
<< /A 48 0 R /Alt (Three-panel line chart comparing net benefit versus threshold probability for clinical decision analysis at twelve months \(panel A, ExtraTrees\), twenty-four months \(panel B, Ridge\), and thirty-six months \(panel C, Ridge\). Each panel compares best model, treating all, and treating none strategies.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 37 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
21 0 obj
<< /A 49 0 R /Alt (Grouped horizontal bar charts labeled A, B, and C compare the top ten features affecting model predictions at 24, 36, and 48 months using mean SHAP values. Across all panels, age is consistently the most influential feature, followed by TNM stage and number of chemotherapy cycles, with minor order variations among sex, GNRI, N stage, T stage, BMI, radiation dose, and PNI. Each feature\220s importance is visually represented by bar length, with all panels sharing a similar pattern.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
22 0 obj
<< /A 50 0 R /Alt (Three horizontal bar charts labeled A, B, and C compare the top ten features by mean SHAP value for predicting outcomes at twelve, twenty-four, and thirty-six months. Each chart shows chemotherapy cycles as the most influential feature, followed by TNM stage, T stage, age, sex, N stage, GNRI, PNI, tumor location, and BMI, with consistent order across all time points. All axes and feature names are clearly labeled.) /K 1 /P 8 0 R /Pg 38 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
23 0 obj
<< /A 51 0 R /Alt (Panel A presents a Kaplan-Meier survival curve for overall survival at twenty-four months and panel B for progression-free survival at twelve months, both stratified by risk group with low risk in red and high risk in blue; the high-risk group shows significantly lower survival probability compared to the low-risk group in both panels, with p-values less than zero point zero zero zero one.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 39 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
